Z||000000||1FST2M6||11-29-2000||08:56 AM||||Very nice guy.. i took him for a slide around the block and made my first appearance on the local show/street race car scene last night too... I pulled into the parking lot of the local Starbucks and was quickly SWARMED by 15-20 import and mustang owners..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> all saying "OOOH what is that"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> Lyndsay, myself, bluepearl, his friend and my friend all just laughed and answered questions about my SHINEY orange toy... Kinda felt bad for BluePearl.. i had intended to go meet with him and spent the first 30+ minutes answering other questions... Thanks for the company and you have my e-mail addy if your ever out and about...||||reg||1
Z||000001||PearlBlueSoul||11-29-2000||10:04 AM||||I gotta say man, that's very nice.  I liked the brakes, the handling, everything about it!  The pictures can't possibly do it any justice.<P>Don't get your hopes up tho.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  That car has the same thing I actually am not fond of in the MKII MR2s, and that's the luxury.  my car's got more of a go-kart feel to it.  I dunno, you'll just have to see it when I get my license back (or when a friend drives it out to barett).  <P>Very nice car, in great shape, love the mods, absolutely gorgious bodywork.  Gotta say man, I'm impressed.  <P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">       <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||14
Z||000002||PearlBlueSoul||11-29-2000||10:09 AM||||1FST2M6, the pics DON'T DO YOUR CAR JUSTICE! I need to get ahold of a camera and shoot your car professionally. <P>I had the esteemed pleasure of riding in this guy's car, and lemme tell ya, it's somethign else. Very clean, well done, and he's still not done with it yet! Man...great car. Wish I could see it in daylight. <P>I will more than definatley take you up on the GZE motor you've got, that and the SC14 upgrade. After that I've got in mind to get a special pulley and some other stuff. This is a very cool thing.  <P>(This was a post you might not have seen...wrote this one the moment I got home.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )           <P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">       <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||1
