Z||000007||PearlBlueSoul||11-29-2000||02:53 PM||||I duno, maybe some people on the MR2 board truly do have a closed mind.  I love seeing modified cars, so that might be part of it, and another is because of it's singularity as one of the few mid engine sports cars, who's layout alone has worn a VERY DEEP hole in my heart.  I don't think I could even have a kid and not have my MR2, I care (dare I say, 'love??') it that much.  <P>I duno, it also is some of the social aspect, because normally people in rare segments of the automotive scene tend to be very knowledgeable and intellectual when it comes to discussing their car (shame to say that's not Always true, perfect example is my home board unfortunatley.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">).  I am very closed minded about going Front wheel, front drive, as I very much don't like the majority of the cars out there with this layout.  I haven't seen one good sportscar (not ECONOMY CAR turned sports car) that I really like far side of a prelude or a Type R (NO LESS!) Integra.  Even those two cars tho, are hondas and hence very common.  Which is why I bite the bullet and stick with soemthing so rare and (sometimes) expensive as this car.  <P>Just wish everyone could see it through the same shade of tinted glass.  <P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">       <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||1
